# poki2.online — Cloudflare Pages redirects
#
# Cloudflare Pages applies ONLY the first 100 redirect declarations in this
# file; #101 and beyond are dropped with no warning, and the request simply
# 404s. Measured on 2026-11-06 (the play host's _redirects had 452
# declarations and its tail had been dead for months — /games/geodash at #100
# answered 301, /games/getaway-shootout at #102 answered 404). This file
# must stay under that ceiling. Only 301/302/303/307/308 are supported; any
# other status code, 410 included, is ignored.
#
# The legacy "/game/* -> https://play.poki2.online/game/:splat" rule was
# removed on 2026-11-06. It was in the first commit, the apex never served a
# /game/ page in any revision, and its destination no longer exists: the play
# catalogue moved to /game/<category>/<slug>/, so every URL it produced
# answered 301 -> 404. A redirect to nothing is worse than an honest 404.
# The legacy shape that does exist is /games/<slug>, which the redirect
# worker serves (poki2.online/games/* -> play.poki2.online/game/<c>/<slug>/).
# If the /game/ shape ever returns to Google's radar, give the worker a
# matching route instead of a splat here — a splat cannot insert the
# category letter, which is why this rule could never be repaired in place.
#
# The 2-player hub moved under the games section on 2026-11-04 (it is a
# catalogue page, so it lives at /fgame/2-player-games). 301 preserves the
# signals IndexNow announced for the old path earlier that day.
/2-player-games   /fgame/2-player-games  301
/2-player-games/  /fgame/2-player-games  301

# Old game index path
/games          https://play.poki2.online/             301
/games/         https://play.poki2.online/             301

